  "body": "Question: are strings like `%6.9f` formatting specifiers?\r\n\r\nAs of commit 79390cb5727d0d89f70cc4902442ae824f010c19 the answer seems to be no, but chrome and firefox both treat it as a specifier:\r\n\r\n```js\r\n> console.log(\"|%6.9f|\",1.23)\r\n|1.23|\r\n```",
